  "result": "Perfect! All 209 tests pass. I've successfully added customer statement functionality:\n\n**New file `src/statements.js`:**\n\n**`statement(customerId, invoices, asOf)`** function:\n- Generates a customer statement as of a specific date\n- Returns `ok({ customerId, invoices, totalDue })` where:\n  - `customerId`: normalized customer ID\n  - `invoices`: array of eligible invoices, each with:\n    - `number`: invoice number\n    - `issueDate`: invoice issue date\n    - `dueDate`: calculated payment due date\n    - `total`: total invoice amount from `invoiceTotals`\n    - `due`: amount still owed from `balanceDue`\n  - `totalDue`: sum of all `due` amounts\n\n**Filtering logic:**\n- Only includes invoices with status 'issued' or 'partially_paid'\n- Only includes invoices with issueDate on or before `asOf` date\n- Filters by customer (normalizes customer ID)\n- Sorts by issueDate (ascending)\n\n**Error handling:**\n- Returns `CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND` if customer doesn't exist\n- Returns `DATE_INVALID` if asOf is not a valid 'YYYY-MM-DD' date\n\n**Key features:**\n- Normalizes customer IDs (handles mixed case and spaces)\n- Integrates with existing payment tracking (via `balanceDue`)\n- Properly handles invoices with multiple partial payments\n- Excludes fully paid invoices from statement\n- Excludes draft invoices from statement\n\n**Tests added (14 new, 209 total):**\n- Empty statement for customer with no invoices\n- Customer not found error\n- ID normalization\n- Invalid date validation\n- Including issued and partially_paid invoices\n- Excluding paid and draft invoices\n- Excluding invoices after asOf date\n- Sorting by issueDate\n- Correct totalDue calculation\n- Partial payment handling\n- DueDate inclusion\n- Multi-customer filtering\n\nAll 209 tests pass. \u2705",
